    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Smart Irrigation Controller (ESP32)\nWaters on soil data and the weather forecast, not on a timer, with a manual override any farmer can use.\n\nThe cloud side of the ESP32 controller in this repo. Point the firmware's WEBHOOK_URL here: each reading is checked (median of 3 sensors vs crop-stage threshold, rain forecast skip, max run time), logged to a sheet, and the farmer gets a WhatsApp message whenever the valve opens. The webhook response tells the device what to do.\n\n**Try it:** click *Test workflow* to run on the sample data. Then connect your credentials on the output nodes and activate.\n\nCode and docs: github.com/Princewill106/smart-irrigation-controller",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 5
      },
